{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ridiculous-expert-mouse","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Eval corpus + ADR-0054 calibration for `project.measurement-provenance`\n\n## Context\n\nStory `f161-c70a-1a69-4ed1` landed the measurement-provenance mechanism: the deterministic\npresence/shape check (`det_measurement_provenance.py`, advisory via `p6_ac_quality`), the\n`.rebar/` overlay routing entry (advisory, `exec: AGENT`, `[operator-attested]` trigger), the\n`execution_mode: agentic` rubric stating decision rules (a)-(d), and ADR-0061.\n\nWhat it did NOT deliver is any proof that the AGENT criterion actually FIRES or STAYS SILENT as\nthe rubric specifies. The rubric states the rules; nothing exercises them. Every sibling project\ncriterion ships a `.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml`; this one has none.\n\nThis was descoped from f161 deliberately: the criterion ships **advisory**, so the mechanism is\ncorrect and useful without calibration, and the ADR-0054 promotion decision it feeds is not being\nmade yet. Filed as an **idea** because promotion is a judgement call nobody has committed to.\n\n## Approach\n\nFollow the `project.engine-layer-enforcement` pattern exactly (`.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-engine-layer-enforcement.eval.yaml`\n+ its offline shape test + a live semantic run recorded as attested evidence).\n\n**1. `.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-measurement-provenance.eval.yaml`** — a BALANCED corpus,\n`epochs: 3`, `gate: at_least(2)`, a deterministic `emits_valid_findings` scorer. Each entry needs a\n`note` naming the causal mechanism and observable effect, not just a label. Minimum fixtures:\n\n| Rule | Fixture | expect |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) environment contradiction | declares `579718921998`, repo Terraform backend names `896586841071` | finding |\n| (a) contrast | declared account MATCHES the IaC | pass |\n| (b) no-anchor fallback | non-AWS cluster/tenant id with no in-repo counterpart | pass |\n| (c) privilege posture | scoped-permission criterion declaring `privilege_posture=broader` | finding |\n| (c) contrast | same criterion declaring `production-equivalent` | pass |\n| (d) instrument vs claim | AUTHORIZATION claim + `instrument=simulation` **at** `privilege_posture=production-equivalent` | finding |\n| (d) contrast | same claim with `instrument=live-call` | pass |\n\nThe (d) must-fire case is the load-bearing one: it is the ONLY fixture that proves `instrument` is\njudged INDEPENDENTLY of `privilege_posture`. Both fields read 'fine' in it, and it must still fire —\nthat is escape 2b (`simulate-principal-policy` returning a confident WRONG authorization answer that\nonly a live call refuted). If this fixture passes when it should fire, the fourth field epic 3147\nmandated is decorative.\n\n**Fixture quality is the actual work.** A must-fire plan so obviously broken that any criterion\nwould flag it proves nothing. Each must-fire case should differ from its contrast case in ONE\ndeclared field, so a fire/pass split isolates the rule under test.\n\n**2. `tests/unit/test_measurement_provenance_eval.py`** — offline shape checks, no LLM, CI-safe:\nfixture parses, ids unique, `criterion` matches, both polarities present, every rule covered.\n\n**3. Live semantic run** — `rebar criteria eval project.measurement-provenance --runs 3`, recorded on\nthis ticket as `[operator-attested]` evidence. Dogfood this epic's own contract: the attestation must\nitself carry a `provenance:` line (environment / principal / privilege_posture / instrument), which\ndoubles as the cheapest possible test that the new four-field contract is writable in practice.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the eval corpus exists with BOTH polarities for each of rules (a), (c) and (d), plus the\n      rule-(b) no-anchor pass case, each carrying a `note` naming the causal mechanism\n- [ ] the rule-(d) must-fire fixture declares `privilege_posture=production-equivalent` AND\n      `instrument=simulation` on an authorization claim, proving `instrument` is judged\n      independently rather than as a proxy for privilege\n- [ ] each must-fire fixture differs from its contrast fixture in exactly ONE declared field, so\n      the fire/pass split isolates the rule under test\n- [ ] an OFFLINE shape test passes with no LLM call: `pytest tests/unit/test_measurement_provenance_eval.py -q`\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the live run `rebar criteria eval project.measurement-provenance --runs 3`\n      is recorded on this ticket with its per-fixture outcomes and the measured FALSE-POSITIVE RATE,\n      and that comment itself carries a `provenance:` line declaring environment, principal,\n      privilege_posture and instrument (dogfooding ADR-0061)\n- [ ] the promotion decision is RECORDED either way: advisory -> blocking with the FP rate that\n      justifies it, or 'stays advisory' with the reason — ADR-0054 requires the evidence, not a\n      particular outcome","id":"98df-3528-9b1f-405a","parent_id":"3147-7b57-5263-4e5d","priority":2,"tags":["gate-rigor","plan-review","evidence-provenance","calibration"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Eval corpus + ADR-0054 calibration for project.measurement-provenance"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785939861212630001,"uuid":"825df933-3747-4539-94b2-3663b3d15a5f"}